    },
    {
      "name": "Berkson's paradox",
      "severity": "CAUTION",
      "assessment": "The fixed, filtered, previously used math/code panel is a selected population. Neither 256 panel requests nor the designed recurrence stream estimates natural conversation traffic."
    },
    {
      "name": "Collider bias",
      "severity": "NOTE",
      "assessment": "Every planned final slot and pre-update row is present and valid, so no success-conditioned subset was used. The selector uses current/past prompt descriptors; final outcomes and labels do not enter the reconstructed choices."
    },
    {
      "name": "Base rate neglect",
      "severity": "CAUTION",
      "assessment": "Final sampling is 128 math plus 128 coding requests, while future events 3-8 contain 256 math and 512 coding. Ratios weight by reference call totals; neither mix is an estimate of deployment prevalence."
    },
    {
      "name": "Regression to the mean",
      "severity": "NOTE",
      "assessment": "Contemporaneous fixed K/U controls and all prespecified events are retained. Samples were not chosen after an extreme efficacy result. Three timing repeats concern the same trained endpoints, not three training replications."
    },
    {
      "name": "Survivorship bias",
      "severity": "NOTE",
      "assessment": "All 2304 final slots, 3072 pre-update generations, four parity controls and 24 worker ledgers reconcile. No invalid, unknown or unattempted final generation is dropped; no unknown worker/root operation remains."
    },
    {
      "name": "Look-elsewhere effect",
      "severity": "CAUTION",
      "assessment": "Pooled R/U is primary; R/K is required. Neither interval excludes zero. Domain, U/K and timing intervals are descriptive and unadjusted; coding R/U alone cannot turn the overall endpoint into a positive result."
    },
    {
      "name": "Garden of forking paths",
      "severity": "CAUTION",
      "assessment": "The presealed recipe, fixed seeds, eight events, 32-record allocation, exact selection and bootstrap agree. No outcome-based rerun appears in this evidence. The reused panel and prior research choices still preclude a fresh confirmatory claim."
    },
    {
      "name": "Correlation versus causation",
      "severity": "CAUTION",
      "assessment": "The controlled R/U contrast compares selectors at the same allocation under shared K-generated supervision. It does not identify why domain effects differ, establish seed robustness, or show asynchronous or training-inclusive speedup. Coverage improved at all seven replay events without a demonstrated overall serving gain."
    },
    {
      "name": "Reverse causality",
      "severity": "NOTE",
      "assessment": "All selected old records precede their training event; admission follows all three commits. Future-serving counts first differ at event 3 after the event-2 update. Temporal order is correct, but it does not prove a general mechanism explanation."
    }
